# Opalescence "does not animate itself, but can be animated by another Opalescence" (the ruling): with two out, each is a
# 4/4 enchantment creature, so Clone may copy one on turn 5. It copies the copiable values only (CR 707.2): Opalescence's,
# a noncreature enchantment with its static ability and its mana cost - not the animation, which is no copiable value. As
# an enchantment the two others make it a creature with base power and toughness its mana value, the copied {2}{W}{W}'s 4
# (CR 202.3, layer 7b), and its own ability animates the two others in turn: three 4/4 enchantment creatures, each named
# Opalescence. Clone's printed 0/0 and its own mana value of 4 play no part.

